<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="32bb139b">&lt;p&gt;
    The change impact analysis approach consists of the rationale and fundamental principles for conducting a robust
    analysis that requires high involvement from business resources. This approach addresses:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The process for conducting an impact analysis
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How to create a change impact analysis finding report, summaries and action plans with key client stakeholders and
        business representatives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        When to complete key tasks, which should be part of the overall project plan and dependencies on process design and
        system requirement completion&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="9517871b"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="93946ff"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="e91aa77f"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="d40f0f53">To define all the steps involved in preparing, conducting, and analyzing and summarizing impact data to gain commitment
from change sponsors to devote business resources needed to participate in all these steps to varying degrees.</attribute>
